# What must not end up in an image that gets pushed to a registry.
#
# `.gitignore` already keeps these out of the repository, and this file is the
# second half of the same rule: a build context is copied from the working tree,
# not from git, so an untracked `.env` sitting next to the Dockerfile is exactly
# the kind of thing that ships to ECR without anyone noticing.

# Credentials. The container gets these from Secrets Manager at run time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Third-party government content. Not ours to redistribute, and the corpus is
# mounted at ARIANE_CORPUS_DIR rather than baked in. See NOTICE and §30.
.ingest/
.firecrawl/
.corpus/
.private/
.graph/
artifacts/

# Rebuilt inside the image, and a host copy is the wrong architecture anyway.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.next/
.expo/
dist/
build/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Internal planning and scratch notes.
plan.md
log.md
version.md
context.md
NOTES.md
SCRATCH.md
TODO.md
*.notes.md
*.plan.md
.claude/

.git/
.github/
.vercel/
coverage/
*.log
